<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Song–Đại Việt war</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1075–1077</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Song–Dai Viet war</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>–Đại Việt war was fought between the Song dynasty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and the Lý dynasty of Đại Việt in 1075–1077. The Vietnamese general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ly-thuong-kiet">Lý Thường Kiệt</a> struck first, raiding Song territory in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guangxi">Guangxi</a> and destroying Yongzhou. A Song counter-invasion was halted at the Như Nguyệt River in 1077, and the war ended in a negotiated peace that left Đại Việt independent.</p></div>
